Search for Subarray
Difficulty: HardAccuracy: 48.11%Submissions: 9K+Points: 8
You are given two integer arrays a[] and b[]. Return all the starting indexes of all the occurences of b[] as a subarray in a[].

Examples:

Input: a[] = [2, 4, 1, 0, 4, 1, 1], b[] = [4, 1]
Output: [1, 4]
Explanation: b[] occurs as a subarray in a[] from index 1 to 2 and from index 4 to 5.


C++//////////////////////////

class Solution {
  public:
    vector<int> search(vector<int> &a, vector<int> &b) {
        vector<int> ans;
        int n = a.size(), m = b.size();

        for (int i = 0; i <= n - m; i++) {
            bool found = true;

            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                if (a[i + j] != b[j]) {
                    found = false;
                    break;
                }
            }

            if (found) ans.push_back(i);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
